An ingest whose next file cannot be created publishes the transient, which
holds every chunk applied so far, so the slice that threw is visible before
resume(). ingest_rotate serves both the mid-slice rotation and the one after
the last chunk.
Guarded-by: "refuse writes: ingest's post-loop rotation cannot create a file, alloc sweep: ingest whose rotation cannot create a file"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp b/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
index 8b83e51..65af3a6 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
+++ b/bytecaskdb/db_replication.cpp
@@ -230,8 +230,9 @@ void DB::ingest_rotate(TransientEngineState &t,
   try {
     rotation = prepare_rotation(t);
   } catch (...) {
-    degrade_from(current,
-                 "ingest post-rotation file creation failed: call resume().");
+    degrade_transient(t, current,
+                      "ingest post-rotation file creation failed: call "
+                      "resume().");
     throw;
   }
   finish_rotation(t, std::move(rotation));
